WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.414 --> 00:00:02.330
METE ATAMEL: Let's see
how to build and launch

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:05.210
an ASP.NET core app
from Google Cloud Shell.

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:08.000
First, start Cloud Shell
from Google Cloud console.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.060
By default, Cloud Shell has
.NET command line tool already

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:11.630
installed.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:15.890
Let's create a folder for our
app and use .NET new -t web

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:18.650
command to create a new web app.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.990
This creates a number
of files for our webapp.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:24.200
Let's open the Orion, Cloud
Shell's browser-based editor,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.370
and edit program.cs file,
and add UseUrls line

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:32.210
to make sure that the
webapp binds to port 8080.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:37.890
Save, and now run .NET
restore to download the new

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.659
dependencies for our app.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:48.380
Finally, execute .NET run
command to compile and run

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.120
our application.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.390
Now do a web preview, and
your ASP.NET core app now

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:56.960
runs on Linux in the cloud.

